    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d402">

                <pb facs="0595" n="573" xml:id="pg573"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">645K.51T3/3–1451: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the United States
                        Representative on the Trusteeship Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sayre</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d402-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-03-14T19:00:00-05:00">March 14, 1951—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>783. For Sayre. Urtel 1261. Dept considers undesirable make any representation to
                    Fr and Brit re Ewe problem at present time. Your statement in TC and text of TC
                    Ees make amply clear urgency of submission by Administering Authorities
                    acceptable substantive recommendations next TC. It is Dept view that Fr and Brit
                    require time to consider what steps they may take next. Meanwhile Dept will be
                    re-examining Ewe question with view to determining most useful role US can play
                    to assist in achievement of practicable solution prior to next GA.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d402-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d402-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated for information to Paris as 4801 and London as 4177.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
